{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>אפתחה</b> — The kamatz of the tav is in ḥatef form because of the guttural letter, like <b>אשמעה</b>. Had it been with a sheva alone, it would have been equal [i.e., equivalent]; but so it is found. The meaning of <b>חידות</b> [riddles] is that they are from of old, and the <b>משל</b> [parable]: like <b>נושקי רומי קשת</b> [those who kiss the bow of Rome], <b>לערוך שלחן</b>, <b>ואש נשקה ביעקב</b>, <b>בחוריו אכלה אש</b>. And the <b>חידות</b>: <b>לחם אבירים אכל איש</b> [the bread of the mighty each man ate], in the manner of <b>מהאכל יצא מאכל</b> [from the eater came forth food]. <b>ויהרג במשמניהם ויתן לשבי עזו</b> — for had it not been explicitly stated in the book of Samuel that the capture of the Ark was the event, the riddle would have been difficult."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "The phrase 'היה שוה רק ככה נמצא' is textually awkward; rendered hyper-literally. The fragment 'מני קדם' (from of old / from antiquity) is retained as in the Hebrew. The identity of the citation 'נושקי רומי קשת' is uncertain but left untranslated as Ibn Ezra quotes it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:57.889079154Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}